practiceProblems.description:
In the last two lessons we learned how to print outputs on multiple lines and how to print text and numbers together.

To print output on multiple lines, we use **PHP_EOL**.
```php
echo 20 . PHP_EOL;
echo 2 + 2 . PHP_EOL;

// Output:
// 20
// 4
```

To print text and number together we can put all of that in a single `echo` statement:
```php
echo "This is lesson " . 3 . " of PHP" . PHP_EOL;

// Output:
// This is lesson 3 of PHP
```

Let us solve a few more problems and then we will understand the structure of PHP code.

